@* Spinner (UI docs). Sections: Usage, Examples, Customization, Styling reference, API, Accessibility, Guidelines. *@

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/icon.css</code></li>
    <li>Tag helper <code>&lt;dnf-spinner&gt;</code> in <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Components/BasicTagHelpers.cs</code></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>An indeterminate loading indicator: something is happening and you don't know for how long. Use the
    <code>&lt;dnf-spinner&gt;</code> tag helper, or a <code>&lt;span class="dnf-spinner"&gt;</code> with a role and a label.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="basic">
    <dnf-spinner />
    <span class="dnf-spinner" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<ui-doc-example id="sizes" title="Sizes" description="Sm (0.875rem), Md (1.25rem, the default) and Lg (2rem with a thicker ring).">
    <dnf-spinner size="Sm" />
    <dnf-spinner />
    <dnf-spinner size="Lg" />
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="label" title="Label" description="label is the accessible name, announced politely; say what is loading.">
    <dnf-spinner label="Loading entries" />
    <dnf-spinner size="Sm" label="Checking the SMTP connection" />
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="with-text" title="With text" description="Next to visible text, hide the spinner from assistive technology and let a status region carry the words." layout="stack">
    <div class="dnf-cluster text-sm text-muted" role="status">
        <span class="dnf-spinner dnf-spinner--sm" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>Loading media…</span>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="in-a-card" title="In a card" description="A centred spinner while a panel's content loads; for page content a skeleton usually reads better." layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-card">
        <div class="dnf-card__header">
            <h3 class="dnf-card__title">Recent deliveries</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-card__body flex justify-center py-8">
            <dnf-spinner size="Lg" label="Loading deliveries" />
        </div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="in-a-button" title="In a button" description="Don't put a spinner in a button by hand: pending replaces the button's leading icon with its own spinner.">
    <dnf-button variant="Primary" icon="save" pending="true">Saving</dnf-button>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="customization">Customization</h2>
<p>The three <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/customization">customization levels</a>, none needing <code>!important</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-tailwind" title="Tailwind utilities" description="An arbitrary property sets the size token for one spinner; spacing utilities place it.">
    <dnf-spinner class="[--dnf-spinner-size:3rem]" label="Loading report" />
    <dnf-spinner size="Sm" class="ms-4" />
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-tokens" title="Component tokens" description="Set --dnf-spinner-size (and the ring colours) in your own (unlayered) CSS to restyle spinners in a scope.">
    <div class="dnf-docs-demo-spinner dnf-cluster">
        <dnf-spinner label="Publishing" />
        <dnf-spinner size="Sm" label="Publishing" />
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-code id="custom-tokens-css" lang="css">
.dnf-docs-demo-spinner .dnf-spinner {
    --dnf-spinner-size: 2.5rem;
    border-top-color: var(--dnf-success);
}
</ui-doc-code>
<p>An unlayered rule beats the size modifiers too, so both spinners above share the new size.</p>

<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-spinner</code></td><td>block</td><td>a <code>--dnf-spinner-size</code> circle: a 2px <code>--dnf-border-strong</code> ring with a <code>--dnf-primary</code> arc, one turn per 0.7s</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-spinner--sm</code></td><td>size</td><td>0.875rem</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-spinner--lg</code></td><td>size</td><td>2rem, 3px ring</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="states">States</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Selector</th><th>Look</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>reduced motion</td><td><code>@@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)</code></td><td>turns slower (1.6s)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="tokens">Tokens</h3>
<p><code>--dnf-spinner-size</code>.</p>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<h3 id="api-spinner"><code>&lt;dnf-spinner&gt;</code></h3>
<ui-doc-api type="typeof(DotNetForge.UI.Components.DnfSpinnerTagHelper)" />
<p>Renders <code>&lt;span class="dnf-spinner" role="status" aria-label="…"&gt;</code>; <code>Xl</code> renders the large size.
    <code>class</code> is appended; other attributes pass through.</p>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li><code>role="status"</code> and <code>aria-label</code> (the tag helper sets both): announced politely. A hand-written
        spinner needs the same.</li>
    <li>When visible text already says what is loading, hide the spinner (<code>aria-hidden="true"</code>) so it is not read twice.</li>
    <li>Under reduced motion the spinner keeps turning, slower - it is the only sign that something happens.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do show a spinner only while something is actually loading.</li>
    <li>Do prefer a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/skeleton">skeleton</a> for page content and a
        <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/progress">progress bar</a> when you know how far it has come.</li>
    <li>Don't put a spinner inside a button by hand - use <code>pending</code> on the <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/button">button</a>.</li>
</ul>
